// test-error
// #1320: analysis is whole-program, so a diagnostic in a-side.cnx and a
// DIFFERENT diagnostic in b-side.cnx are both reported in ONE run.
//
// This passed before the hoist too, because the per-file loop recorded each
// file's result and kept walking. It is asserted here because the hoist is what
// makes it STRUCTURAL rather than incidental: 2.1 Analyze now runs over every
// file before any file is planned, so "both are reported" no longer depends on
// how far the emission loop got before the first rejection.
//
// The regression it catches is an analysis pass that stops at the first file it
// rejects -- which is what "analysis is a pass" invites and what the per-file
// early return used to do for the REST of that file's diagnostics.
#include <a-side.cnx>
#include <b-side.cnx>

u32 main() {
    return 0;
}
